<title>CHINA: China PICC Property 1996 auto premiums up 14.3 pct.</title>
<headline>China PICC Property 1996 auto premiums up 14.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The automobile premium income of the People's Insurance Company of China (Property) reached 21 billion yuan ($2.5 billion) in 1996, up 14.3 percent compared with the previous year, the Financial News said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Total insured automobiles reached 10.04 million with the payment ratio at 61.08 percent, down 3.4 percentage points compared with 1995, it said.</p>
<p>PICC Property, one of state-run PICC's three main subsidiaries, reported 35 billion yuan in premiums last year.</p>
<p>($1.0 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
